  "about": "Pinyin (Mandarin, tone marks) shown under Traditional Chinese text when Chinese is the language being learned (Stage 4c, 4 Nov 2026; see docs/guides/ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW_PART1.md#adding-or-changing-a-language). Read by the Lexicon and turned into a reading by rules_zh.gd reading(): text is split into the longest entries of 'words' (and the zh names in names.json); runs of numerals become number words; any other character uses 'chars'. 'chars' gives each character's default reading (citation tone); 'words' gives whole words, including neutral tones (爸爸 bàba), the right reading of characters with several (年長 niánzhǎng, 做得好 zuò de hǎo) and capitals for proper nouns. Tone changes of 一 and 不 are not written (citation tones). The language check fails when a character of the Chinese text has no reading. Claude's draft for review.",
